{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeDim3Indep","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeDim3Indep","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.BurnsideSpan","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeDim3"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sixWords_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sixWords_indep","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeDim3Indep.lean#L142-L150","doc":"**The six words `{1,σ₀,σ₁,σ₀σ₁,σ₁σ₀,σ₀σ₁σ₀}` are linearly independent over `ℝ`**\n(`q ≠ 0`), so `dim_ℝ H_3(q) ≥ 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sixCoeffs_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sixCoeffs_zero","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeDim3Indep.lean#L35-L140","doc":"**Component core.** Given that the three representations `rhoTriv, rhoSign,\nseminormalRep21` each send `c₁·1 + c₂σ₀ + c₃σ₁ + c₄σ₀σ₁ + c₅σ₁σ₀ + c₆σ₀σ₁σ₀`\nto zero, all six coefficients vanish (`q ≠ 0`).  This is the `6×6` solve; both the\nlinear-independence statement and the injectivity of the product representation\nreduce to it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}